-- docs/adr/0001-workspace-ownership.md --
# ADR-0001: Workspace Ownership

* **Status**: Accepted
* **Date**: 2026-10-21

<!-- semedit-adr-metadata:v1 keys=summary,description,role,scope,area,languages; do not change key names or order. -->
| Key | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| summary | Preserve ownership boundaries at the workspace level. |
| description | Keep workspace ownership explicit for maintainers. |
| role | first-principle |
| scope | project |
| area | backend |
| languages | go |

## Context

Workspace ownership defines the boundary for code changes.

## Decision

Keep ownership boundaries explicit.

## Invariants

* Requests stay within their workspace.

## Consequences

Owners can reason about the affected source.
-- docs/adr/0002-code-ownership.md --
# ADR-0002: Code Ownership

* **Status**: Proposed
* **Date**: 2026-10-21

<!-- semedit-adr-metadata:v1 keys=summary,description,role,scope,area,languages; do not change key names or order. -->
| Key | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| summary | Preserve ownership boundaries for code maintainers. |
| description | Keep source-code ownership explicit for maintainers. |
| role | principle |
| scope | source-code |
| area | backend |
| languages | go |

## Context

Several code changes need an explicit owner.

## Decision

Keep ownership boundaries explicit during backend edits.

```text
FencedDecisionNeedle
```

## Invariants

* The code owner remains discoverable. Invariantneedle describes the preserved boundary.

## Consequences

Ownership stays visible to maintainers.
-- docs/adr/0003-ownership-boundaries.md --
